Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sbs-battery: report ENODATA when the
 bridge refuses RunTimeToEmpty

On Krane the battery sits behind the ChromeOS EC I2C tunnel, which
answers register 0x11 with -EIO. power_supply_uevent() aborts on any
error except -ENODATA/-ENODEV, so `cat uevent` was empty and every
battery change uevent was dropped. healthd only saw changes on its
poll timer or on charger events.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sbs-battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/sbs-battery.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sbs-battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sbs-battery.c
@@ -987,6 +987,14 @@
 			break;
 
 		ret = sbs_get_battery_property(client, ret, psp, val);
+		/*
+		 * The ChromeOS EC I2C tunnel on Krane refuses RunTimeToEmpty
+		 * (0x11) with -EIO. An error other than -ENODATA makes the
+		 * power supply core drop the whole uevent, so battery changes
+		 * never reach userspace. Report no data for it instead.
+		 */
+		if (ret == -EIO && psp == POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_EMPTY_NOW)
+			return -ENODATA;
 		break;
 
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_MODEL_NAME:
